<concept id="d85aA" xml:lang="en">
   <title>Connecting to your Environment from Excel</title>
   <prolog>
      <author>Rakesh Singh</author>
      <critdates>
         <created date="Jul 28, 2022"/>
      </critdates>
      <metadata>
         <prodinfo>
            <prodname>X-Author for Excel</prodname>
         </prodinfo>
      </metadata>
   </prolog>
   <conbody>
      <p>Now that you have installed X-Author for Excel, you need to open Excel and connect X-Author to your environment. You can create multiple connections to your environment, switch between instances without leaving Excel, and revoke existing connections.</p>
      <p>
         <ul>
            <li>
               <xref href="connecting_to_salesforce_from_excel.dita#ConnectingtoyourEnvironmentfromExcel_ConnectingtoSalesforcefromExcel">Connecting to Salesforce from Excel</xref>
            </li>
            <li>
               <xref href="connecting_to_microsoft_dynamics_from_excel.dita#ConnectingtoyourEnvironmentfromExcel_ConnectingtoMicrosoftDynamicsfromExcel">Connecting to Microsoft Dynamics from Excel</xref>
            </li>
            <li>
               <xref href="connecting_to_apttus_omni_from_excel.dita#ConnectingtoyourEnvironmentfromExcel_ConnectingtoApttusOmnifromExcel">Connecting to Apttus Omni from Excel</xref>
            </li>
            <li>
               <xref href="adding_more_connections.dita#ConnectingtoyourEnvironmentfromExcel_AddingMoreConnections">Adding More Connections</xref>
            </li>
            <li>
               <xref href="switching_connections.dita#ConnectingtoyourEnvironmentfromExcel_SwitchConnect">Switching Connections</xref>
            </li>
            <li>
               <xref href="revoking_connections.dita#ConnectingtoyourEnvironmentfromExcel_RevokingConnections">Revoking Connections</xref>
            </li>
         </ul>
      </p>
   </conbody>
